# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.23-native-aitia-backpressure-content-review.org::#persistent-owner-recovery
# render-layout: elk; theme: 0; pad: 24; timeout: 30
direction: down
producer: "Process A: existing native Aitia owner\nReal ASCENT union + complete signed decision inventory\nSeal retires known live ancestors and owner before IO"
archive: "Closed archive\nCanonical native cut + all records / origins / references\nOriginal signed targets stay historical\nNo native receipt authority is serialized"
host: "Existing trusted host\nSelect latest immutable signed head by independent digest\nSealed -> activate one fresh process incarnation\nAn active missing owner cannot be replaced from an old seal"
restart: "Process B: real restart / explicit optional archive import\nOne-time native crypto reader identity; saved labels refused\nOne source binds one actual owner\nNew native ASCENT registration and queries\nExact finite footprint comparison\nSame source / methods / obligations required for reuse"
native: "Existing Aitia and Core\nMandatory archived predecessor source\nSame handover admission path and original signature verification\nNo public intake acknowledgment before activated handover\nFresh local requests and genuine new receipts"
gate: "Current-use review gate\nComplete current history + named disposition -> admitted\nUnresolved verified counter -> rejected\nAbsent / incomplete / stale history -> pending\nOld receipt presentations cannot authorize recovery"
expanded: "Process B receives another counter\nOld positive does not close new negative\nSeal expanded inventory -> process C rechecks\nUnsealed exit -> process D stays pending"
reject: "Refused archive input\nOmitted record / target mismatch / wrong cut\nValid old head fails latest host pin\nNo fallback that erases historical failures"
reuse: "Evidence reuse\nKeep exact real Rust / QNT / Lean method artifacts\nRestore identical required bytes -> recheck applicability\nChanged current source still blocks mechanical admission"
boundary: "Qualification boundary\nFour actual Scheme processes / 21 gold outcomes\nLocal test-only Ed25519 principals\nNo power-loss, WAL, multi-writer CAS or atomic external effect"
producer -> archive
host -> restart
archive -> restart -> native -> gate
host -> native
archive -> reject -> gate
native -> expanded -> host: "new closed checkpoint or pending"
gate -> reuse -> boundary
